                        "sense_id": "0c9c0c63-2015-3353-afd5-0d4d59958710",
                        "entry_id": "7ccba3be-3789-32d0-99fa-fcd2909ca592",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any species of the family Cercopithecidae, the Old World monkeys."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c61b0b84-6d03-4cc0-ad4b-3447528a590e",
                                "sense_id": "0c9c0c63-2015-3353-afd5-0d4d59958710",
                                "text": "In the rhesus monkey, proboscis monkey, and gibbon, representatives of cercopithecids and hylobatids, respectively, neonatal cranial dimensions approach the corresponding pelvic inlet dimensions, however, without exceeding them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a77cd6d5-00fa-44a8-bc8d-c267a1dff744",
                                "sense_id": "0c9c0c63-2015-3353-afd5-0d4d59958710",
                                "text": "2011, Terry Harrison, Chapter 6: Cercopithecids (Cercopithecidae, Primates), Terry Harrison (editor), Paleontology and Geology of Laetoli: Human Evolution in Context, Volume 2: Fossil Hominins and the Associated Fauna, page 134,\nMore importantly, perhaps, is the observation that cercopithecids are significantly under-represented in the lowermost horizons of the Upper Laetolil Beds below Tuff 5."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "50f173fa-532c-44e0-818f-8672feb6cc62",
                                "sense_id": "0c9c0c63-2015-3353-afd5-0d4d59958710",
                                "text": "In North Africa, cercopithecids assigned to the genus Prohylobates are known from two Early Miocene localities: Wadi Moghara, Egypt (Simons 1969), and Gebel Zelten, Libya (Delson 1979)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
